# Template for the secret env vars the two workflows need.
# Copy to `.env`, fill in real values, then push to EAS as SECRET env vars:
#   eas env:push production --path .env        # choose "Secret" visibility for each
# `.env` is gitignored; this `.env.default` is committed as the reference.
#
# Provider credentials used by the harness:
#   - CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN: a long-lived subscription OAuth token generated
#     by `claude setup-token`. Used by Claude Code authoring and the evaluator's
#     claude-agent-sdk loop. Requires Claude Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise.
#   - OPENAI_API_KEY: used by Codex (telemetry workflow; e2e with AGENT=codex).
#   - AGENT_MODEL: optional model override for eval-e2e. Defaults to `sonnet`
#     for Claude Code and `gpt-5-mini` for Codex.
#   - EXPO_TOKEN: an Expo Robot User access token (expo.dev account/org settings
#     -> Robot users; needs at least the "Publish and view all projects" role).
#     Expo CLI treats this as a full non-interactive substitute for `eas login` --
#     no login step needed once it's set. Two uses: (1) lets the coding agent
#     run its own `eas init`/`eas build` self-verification step during
#     authoring (see eval_harness/prompts/author_app.md) -- if unset, that
#     self-check fails and reports it rather than silently skipping; (2) is used
#     directly as the Expo MCP server's bearer token (mcp.expo.dev now accepts
#     an Expo Robot User access token as-is -- no separate OAuth login/refresh
#     dance needed; see eval::configure_expo_mcp in agents.sh).
#
# Expo project routing is configurable through app.config.js:
#   - EAS_PROJECT_ID: optional EAS project UUID override. Defaults to the current
#     Georgian test project id committed in app.config.js.
#   - EXPO_SLUG: optional Expo project slug override.
#   - EXPO_OWNER: optional Expo owner/account override.
#
# The end-to-end workflow (eval-e2e.yml) also uses, all OPTIONAL:
#   - GCS_BUCKET + GCP_SA_KEY: optional mirror for the per-run bundle. EAS job
#     artifacts are the primary download path; GCS is only for longer retention
#     or external processing. GCP_SA_KEY is the full service-account JSON.
#   - BRAINTRUST_API_KEY: if set, reconstructed agent traces and evaluator traces
#     are also pushed to Braintrust.
#   - BRAINTRUST_PROJECT: Braintrust project for traces (default expo-evals).
#     BRAINTRUST_CC_PROJECT / BRAINTRUST_EVAL_PROJECT can override agent/evaluator
#     traces separately if needed.
#   - PUSH_EVAL_TRACE_BT: opt into the legacy evaluator-trace mirroring script.
#     Default is off because evaluator Claude SDK conversations are emitted as
#     the primary "Agentic Evaluator Session" trace.

CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- optional (eval-e2e.yml) ---
# EXPO_TOKEN=...
# EAS_PROJECT_ID=338f6455-57a3-49c9-a2e0-36e5a0577c77
# EXPO_SLUG=adi-test-project
# EXPO_OWNER=georgian-team
# AGENT_MODEL=sonnet
# GCS_BUCKET=my-eval-artifacts
# GCP_SA_KEY={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...", ...}
# BRAINTRUST_API_KEY=sk-...
# BRAINTRUST_PROJECT=expo-evals
# BRAINTRUST_CC_PROJECT=expo-evals
# BRAINTRUST_EVAL_PROJECT=expo-evals
# PUSH_EVAL_TRACE_BT=0
